You are a fork of the corpus agent. Execute directly — do not spawn agents. Eight other forks are writing the other files in parallel; write ONLY the 5 files listed under YOUR FILES, into /tmp/corpus2/md/. Do not create helper/scratch files anywhere, do not read or modify anything under /workspace or /tmp/corpus (never glob /tmp/corpus*), and never run a formatter or R/knitr.

HOW TO WRITE: one Write tool call per file with the full content (plain UTF-8, LF, final newline). The Bash tool here refuses heredocs/printf/compound commands — use Bash only for the validator below; fix problems with Edit.

SIZE: every file 80-300 lines; aim for the range given per file.

REALISM: hand-written-looking R Markdown documents by plausible (fictional) authors, with plausible data, packages, citation keys, dates. Every file distinct in structure.

GENERAL MARKDOWN MESSINESS to sprinkle in (each file at least ~8): nested bullet lists (2- and 4-space indents, mixed markers), numbered lists (incl. starting at a number other than 1, `1)` delimiters, `1.`/`1.`/`1.`), task lists, pipe tables (alignment colons, ragged pipes, inline code, wide cells), blockquotes (multi-paragraph, nested), HTML comments, ATX headings with trailing `#` and setext headings, emphasis `_x_`/`__x__`/`*x*`/`**x**`, long inline URLs, reference links with definitions at the bottom, footnotes, thematic breaks `***`/`___`/`- - -`, hard breaks (two trailing spaces / backslash), stray trailing spaces, inconsistent blank lines (2-3 in a row in places), non-ASCII (é, ü, µ, ±, —, …).

R MARKDOWN SPECIFICS: front matter with `output:` options (html_document toc/toc_float/code_folding/df_print, bookdown::pdf_document2, rmarkdown::html_vignette, github_document, word_document + pdf_document), `params:`, quoted inline-R date in YAML (`date: "`r format(Sys.Date(), '%d %B %Y')`"`); editor options vary exactly as specified per file below. Chunks with headers like `{r setup, include=FALSE}`, `{r revenue-trend, echo=FALSE, fig.cap="...", fig.width=8}`, `{r, eval = FALSE}`, `{r tbl-demo, results='asis'}`; inline `` `r expr` ``; bookdown refs `\@ref(fig:x)`, `(ref:label)` text references, `(\#eq:x)`; `{-}` unnumbered headings, `{.tabset}`. PROSE: long multi-sentence paragraphs full of abbreviations and sentence-boundary traps (e.g., i.e., Dr., Prof., Mr., Fig., Figs., Eq., et al., vs., approx., ca., cf., No., Inc., U.S., St., p.m., decimals like 3.5 mL and p < 0.05, ellipses, sentences ending in `?`, `!`, `."`, `.)`), and numbered/bulleted lists whose items contain several sentences. Files with `wrap: sentence` must NOT already be one-sentence-per-line everywhere — mix sentence-per-line lines with multi-sentence lines and mid-sentence breaks; the `wrap: 72` file is mostly (imperfectly) wrapped at 72; the `wrap: none` file has long single-line paragraphs. Code fences/chunks must close; front matter must be valid YAML.

YOUR FILES (/tmp/corpus2/md/):
1. quarterly-sales-report.Rmd (~160-240 lines) — `title` with an em dash, `author`, quoted inline-R `date`, `output: html_document:` (toc, `toc_float: { collapsed: false }` or block form, number_sections, df_print paged, code_folding hide, theme, highlight), `params:` (region "EMEA", quarter 2), `editor_options:\n  chunk_output_type: console\n  markdown:\n    wrap: sentence`. Body: setup chunk with `knitr::opts_chunk$set(...)`, `{r load-data, cache=TRUE}`, `{r revenue-trend, fig.cap="Monthly revenue by channel, Q2 2024."}`, `{r top-products, results='asis'}`, inline `` `r scales::dollar(total_rev)` ``, `## Regional breakdown {.tabset}` with `### EMEA` etc., long multi-sentence paragraphs (e.g., i.e., Dr. Patel, Fig. 2, et al., vs., approx., Inc., U.S., No. 3, 4 p.m.), numbered + bulleted lists with multi-sentence items, kable tables.
